  "notes": {
    "t1": { "x": 0, "y": -300, "text": "Foundations — the system, and every state money can be in", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 2560 },
    "t2": { "x": 0, "y": 940,  "text": "Onboarding — Phase 1, the set nobody had drawn", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 2270 },
    "t3": { "x": 0, "y": 2140, "text": "The requester loop — Phase 2", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 2270 },
    "t4": { "x": 0, "y": 3340, "text": "Delivery, the doer side, the money — Phase 2 into 3", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 2270 },
    "t5": { "x": 0, "y": 4540, "text": "Later — carried over, but not before Phase 4", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 2740 },
    "n1": { "x": 2400, "y": 1240, "w": 320, "text": "Phase 1 exits when a doer can register, pass KYC and appear in a list. These five screens are exactly that — and none of the four earlier canvases contained a single one of them.\n\nScreen 5 is the one that matters. The failure path is the common path: a name that doesn't match, a verifier that can't decide. Each state names what went wrong and the one thing to do next." },
    "n2": { "x": 2400, "y": 2440, "w": 320, "text": "No booking fee on the requester side. The 18% comes out of the doer's payout, so the price posted is the price paid — that is ADR-0002 made visible.\n\nOne earlier canvas charged the requester a fee at this step. It contradicts the fee decision, so it is not carried over." }
